data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"The value of a state under a fixed policy is the expected reward now, plus the discounted value\nof wherever you land next. Two averages are hidden in that sentence: one over the actions the\npolicy picks, and one over the next states the transitions pick. Averaging the actions first\nturns the problem into a smaller one with a single transition matrix."},"hints_note":null}

